# Phase 18 factory per-client NameServer discovery parity

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 09:38:42 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Implementation revision: `df87b7b2`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Scope: `MQClientAPIFactory` domain discovery and refresh address ownership

## Finding and change

Pinned Java `MQClientAPIFactory.createAndStart` calls `fetchNameServerAddr`
on each newly created API client. `MQClientAPIImpl` stores the discovered
string in its own `nameSrvAddr`, and scheduled refresh calls that same API
instance. Rust previously stored one factory-wide current string and
broadcast every slot's discovery response to all started clients. The factory
now tracks one current address per pool index; startup and refresh responses
update only that slot. Explicit factory address-change calls continue to
update every client.

The invoked Java fixture starts two domain clients against a bounded local HTTP
responder. Its responses are `127.0.0.11:9876` and `127.0.0.12:9876`; the
observed client address lists preserve those separate values. The Rust
`factory_domain_discovery_keeps_each_clients_address_independent` regression
consumes the same fixture.

